  "content": {
    "title": "Arkansas vs High Point live updates: Score, highlights of March Madness Round 2 game",
    "text": "Updated March 22, 2026, 12:00 a.m. ETFollow all of Saturday's NCAA Tournament second round games with USA TODAY Sports' live updates.PORTLAND, OR — The clock has struck midnight for High Point.Despite a valiant effort from the 12th seeded Panthers, No. 4 seed Arkansas came out on top of a thrilling shootout, winning 94-88 to advance to the Sweet 16.Fresh off taking down No. 5 seed Wisconsin in a dramatic first round win, High Point came in ready to play, giving Arkansas all it can handle. It was a back-and-forth game with 3-pointers going down all night, but freshman Darius Acuff Jr. came up clutch again to push the Razorbacks to victory with his late heroics.It was another big night for the guard with a game-high 36 points, with nine of those points coming in the final three minutes. High Point had its own elite guard play from Rob Martin, who poured in 30 points and despite falling short, got a standing ovation from the crowd before the game ended.John Calipari and Arkansas are now back in the Sweet 16 for back-to-back seasons, and it awaits the winner of Arizona and Utah State on Thursday, March 26.Here's a recap of Saturday's second round game.HIT REFRESH FOR UPDATES. High Point vs Arkansas live scoreTEAMS1H2HTOTALHigh Point424688Arkansas435194 High Point vs Arkansas live updates Darius Acuff Jr hits big 3-pointerThe dagger may have been hit. Acuff knocks down a 3-pointer in the final minute to make it a seven point lead. Arkansas pulls ahead in final minutesThe Razorbacks are close to escaping this one. They lead 87-83 with 90 seconds left after Darius Acuff Jr. extends the lead with his 31st point of the night. Arkansas-High Point coming down to wireHigh Point won't go away.After Arkansas used a 10-2 run to get an seven point lead, High Point has punched back to make it a three point deficit at the final media timeout with 3:42 left in the game. 3-pointers flyingIt's absolute bedlam in Portland as both teams are trading 3-pointers. There have been six in the last four minutes, getting the crowd roaring with each one as its tied with just under 10 minutes to go. Trevon Brazile takes hard hitOne of Arkansas' key players is in the locker room after taking a hit. Brazile had the ball when he tripped, and as he fell, High Point's Owen Aquino ran into him. He was on the ground for a few moments during a timeout and was taken to locker room.He returned a few minutes later. Arkansas-High Point trading bucketsThe two teams are still keeping close. Arkansas started the second half with a 7-2 run but High Point responded. Second half underwayThe final 20 minutes have started in this close battle. Halftime: Arkansas 43, High Point 42It was a thrilling first half with High Point still riding the momentum from its first round upset, down by one point to the Razorbacks in a game that had five lead changes.Like in the first round, High Point is riding the 3-pointer, with six deep shots knocked down already. Arkansas has hit four, and are getting to the rim for dunks. High Point's Cam'Ron Fletcher has a game-high 17 points, while Darius Acuff Jr. leads Arkansas with 13 points. High Point knocking down 3-pointersAfter starting 1-for-10 from deep, High Point is starting to make its 3-pointers. It's made four since then and it's got the Panthers down by one point with 4:30 left in the first half. Arkansas, High Point tip offWe're underway in Portland, and the Panthers and Razorbacks will look for a bid in the Sweet 16. High Point vs Arkansas nearly underwayRound 1 Cinderella High Point is looking to make a huge splash, as it takes on John Calipari and Arkansas. Tip-off is just around the corner.What time is Arkansas vs High Point?Time: 9:45 p.m. ET, Saturday.What channel is Arkansas vs High Point? How to watch, streaming infoThe game is airing on TBS/truTV, streaming via Fubo. Where is High Point?High Point University is located in High Point, North Carolina, southwest of Greensboro.Arkansas vs High Point prediction, oddsEhsan Kassim: ArkansasJordan Mendoza: ArkansasJohn Leuzzi: ArkansasBlake Schuster: High PointMoneyline: Arkansas (-1300)Spread: Arkansas (-13)Over/under total: 169.5Darius Acuff Jr. 2026 NBA Draft mock draft predictionNo. 6 overall to Dallas MavericksKalbrosky's Analysis:Now led by Cooper Flagg, the Mavericks need to find players who can help Dallas stay competitive on offense and Arkansas freshman Darius Acuff Jr. can do exactly that. The SEC Player of the Year is excellently efficient at operating ball screens or in isolation. He leads freshmen for points created per 40 minutes (43.1) either by himself or through an assist, per CBB Analytics. He can score well from either side of the court and is among the freshmen leaders in both alley-oop assists (15) and field goals made in transition (62) this season. There is a reason rival coach Sean Miller thinks this generational guard should have his name in the mix at No. 1 overall.See USA TODAY's full mock draft hereDarius Acuff Jr. stats(all stats as of March 15)22.9 points per game3.2 rebounds per game6.5 assists per game48.6% field goal percentage44.5% three-point field goal percentageWho is High Point March Madness hero Chase Johnston?Johnston is a seventh-year senior guard for High Point, who entered the Panthers' first-round win over Wisconsin on March 19 averaging 6.1 points and an assist per game on 47.1% shooting.He's on the court for one reason: to shoot 3-pointers. In fact, his game-winning transition layup against the Badgers with 11 seconds remaining was his first 2-point shot of the entire season. He averages 4.3 field goals per game in 2025-26, 4.1 of which are from 3-point range.Johnston is, expectedly, prolific from distance. He's shooting a ridiculous 48.5% from 3-point range this season, and has a 39.8% mark on 3-pointers for his career.To put his role into further perspective, he entered the game with only four 2-point attempts on the season, with four free-throw attempts, all of which he made.Johnston is in his second season at High Point after transferring from Florida Gulf Coast, where he spent two seasons. He saw his first career action at Stetson and averaged 13.5 points and 15.2 points in his first two seasons with the Hatters, respectively, although he spent the fall semester in 2019 at Purdue-Fort Wayne.Who is High Point coach Flynn Clayman?Clayman is in his first season as High Point’s case, having assumed the role after Alan Huss left after last season to become the associate head coach and head-coach-in-waiting at Creighton, his alma mater.Clayman had been Huss’ top assistant for the previous two seasons, a time in which the Panthers went 56-15 and made one NCAA tournament appearance. When Huss left, Clayman was promoted.“As associate head coach, Flynn Clayman has played a pivotal role in HPU's recruiting and offensive success during the past two seasons,\" High Point president Nido Qubein said when Clayman was hired. \"Players appreciate his leadership, and his values align with the values of our university. We are excited to have him lead the men's basketball program as head coach.\"Clayman has made the most of the opportunity, improving to 30-4 this season after the win over Wisconsin. The 30 wins are a single-season program record and the NCAA tournament victory was the first in High Point’s history.",
